period of cos(x):
  fundamental period 2*pi ≈ 6.283185307
  proved symbolically: cos(x) has period 2*pi; x occurs only inside them, so f(x + p) = f(x).  Smallest: no p/k (2 <= k <= 64) is a period (checked at 997 points)
> period tan(x: real)
period of tan(x):
  fundamental period pi ≈ 3.141592654
  proved symbolically: tan(x) has period pi; x occurs only inside them, so f(x + p) = f(x).  Smallest: no p/k (2 <= k <= 64) is a period (checked at 997 points)
> bounded tanh(x: real)
bounded tanh(x):
  bounded (on all real x)
  above: proved by interval arithmetic: f <= 1; the largest value seen is 0.9999999959 at x = 10
  below: proved by interval arithmetic: f >= -1; the smallest value seen is -0.9999999959 at x = -10
